# Real-device test harness. Written as a throwaway for the 7.1 port, and not
# throwaway any more: in September 2026 it caught three defects that would
# otherwise have shipped -- two tiers that could not load at all, and a primary
# artifact that crashed inside the emulator's binary translator. Neither the
# compiler nor CI could see any of them.
#
# It is tracked now, minus everything generated.
#
# WARNING: the .aar under test NEVER enters this tree. This repo is public and the
# harness also tests paid tiers, so it takes the artifact by path:
#
#     ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug -PtestAar=/absolute/path/to/ffmpeg-kit.aar
#
# A CI check would not protect this. It runs AFTER the push, when the file is
# already public, and rewriting history does not truly purge GitHub -- this project
# learned that in July 2026. The only real protection is that the file is never
# copied in. app/libs/ stays ignored as a second line, for hand-run experiments.
/test-app/app/libs/
/test-app/**/build/
# Un repertoire de sortie par palier teste : sur Windows, un processus Java
# resident garde app-debug.apk verrouille et Gradle echoue a effacer sa propre
# sortie. Voir test-app/app/build.gradle.kts, -PbuildTag.
/test-app/**/build-*/
/test-app/.gradle/
/test-app/.kotlin/
/test-app/local.properties

# Internal project notes (Gumroad IDs, pricing, secrets names) - not for a public repo
CLAUDE.md

# Les AAR que le workflow de publication telecharge depuis la release, puis publie
# tels quels. Deux versions 6.0.3 y ont ete SUIVIES par git jusqu'au 2026-09-26 :
# perimees, porteuses du defaut RELRO, et l'une sans libc++_shared.so. Seul le refus
# d'ecrasement de `gh release download` a empeche 6.0.4 de partir avec ces octets-la,
# definitivement -- Maven Central est immuable. Un binaire dans l'arbre est une
# reponse prete a servir a une question que personne ne pose plus.
/android-*-lts/android/ffmpeg-kit-android-lib/prebuilt-aars/
